IMPORT `oa1-related`

-- Old Age Security Act, R.S.C. 1985, c. O-9 -- THE SEAT LAYER for the first piece (title and s 1, Part I, Part IV, Related Provisions).
-- Plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation made by legalese commons; not an official version.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is 65 or older, or approaching 65, asking about the monthly pension (Part I) and about what Part IV (General) means for
-- them: applying and waiving, incapacity and death, reconsideration and appeal, being paid too much, what can be done to them for false information,
-- and when the Minister may inspect documents or enter their home. The Guaranteed Income Supplement and the Allowances (Parts II and III) are asked
-- about in the second piece's seat layer; the Regulations in the third's. There is no seat for an official: the Minister's duties and powers
-- appear below only as what the person is owed or exposed to.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, a number, a date) worded as the person would be asked. The records the layer-1 modules expect
-- (`s 3: Facts of age and residence`, `Sentence of imprisonment`, ...) are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME
-- layer-1 rule is then called; no rule is restated here. Where the Minister's satisfaction or a regulation decides something, the question asks for it as
-- a fact ("Is the Minister satisfied that ...?", "Do the regulations let ...?"); nothing is guessed.
-- Figures the Act leaves to the regulations (the earlier effective days of s 8, the time for cancelling a pension in s 9.3, the manner of the quarterly
-- adjustment) are asked as inputs; a different figure in the regulations would change those answers. The Old Age Security Regulations are the third
-- piece's, and nothing here reads them.
-- The full monthly pension is worked out by the Act from the January-March 1985 figure and the quarterly adjustments; the person cannot state it, so the
-- questions on the amount ask for the published figure for the month.
--
-- No question names these rules, which are encoded in layer 1: s 27 (how the basis of the Consumer Price Index is changed), the three definitions of s 33(1),
-- ss 39 and 40(1) (the Minister's agreements with provinces and with other countries), s 41(2) (notice of an agreement), s 42 and s 43 (how Parliament may
-- disapprove an order), ss 45, 46 and 47 (the fund payments come out of, who administers the Act, the Minister's annual report) and the definitions in s 44.2(1).
-- Rules that a question calls reach the rest (for example s 3(1)(b)(iii) through s 3(1)).
-- Sections 34, 34.2, 40(2), 42(3) to (6) and 1830 of 2010, c. 12, and the amendments not in force, are inert (NOTES.md, "Coverage table").

§ `Old Age Security Act, Part I -- the questions of a person who is 65 or older (or about to be) about the pension`

§§ `Do I qualify for a pension?`

-- s 3(1). A "full monthly pension" is paid to a person who (a) was already a pensioner on July 1, 1977, or (b) was 25 or older in 1977, lived in Canada
-- (or had, or held a visa), is 65 and has lived in Canada for the last ten years (or enough of them), or (c) is 65 and has lived in Canada for 40 years
-- after turning 18. The facts are the ones the Act tests; each question below asks the same ones.
@export Am I qualified for a full monthly pension (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day my application is approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day is (or will) your application for the pension be approved? (If you are asking about now, give today's date.)
      `my application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had your application for an old age pension been approved by July 1, 1977?
      `I lived in Canada on July 1, 1977` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you live in Canada on July 1, 1977?
      `I had lived in Canada for any period after turning 18 before that` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you did not live in Canada on July 1, 1977: had you lived in Canada for any period after turning 18?
      `I held a valid immigration visa on July 1, 1977` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you hold a valid immigration visa on July 1, 1977?
      `I lived in Canada for the ten years just before the day my application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you live in Canada for the ten years immediately before the day your application is approved?
      `years I was present in Canada after turning 18 and before those ten years` IS A NUMBER @desc In total, how many years were you present in Canada after turning 18 and before those ten years? (0 if none)
      `years I was absent from Canada during those ten years` IS A NUMBER @desc In total, how many years were you absent from Canada during those ten years? (0 if none)
      `I lived in Canada for at least one year just before the day my application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you live in Canada for at least one year immediately before the day your application is approved?
      `years I have lived in Canada after turning 18 and before the day my application is approved` IS A NUMBER @desc In total, how many years have you lived in Canada after turning 18 and before the day your application is approved?
      `I was living in Canada on the day before my application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you living in Canada on the day before your application is approved?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1): Am I qualified for a full monthly pension` IF
    `s 3(1): a full monthly pension may be paid to the person` `my age and residence facts`
    WHERE
        `my age and residence facts` MEANS `s 3: Facts of age and residence` WITH
            `the date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `the day on which the person's application is approved` IS `the day my application is approved`
            `the person's application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977` IS `my application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977`
            `resided in Canada on July 1, 1977` IS `I lived in Canada on July 1, 1977`
            `had resided in Canada for any period after attaining eighteen years of age` IS `I had lived in Canada for any period after turning 18 before that`
            `possessed a valid immigration visa on July 1, 1977` IS `I held a valid immigration visa on July 1, 1977`
            `resided in Canada for the ten years immediately preceding the day on which the person's application is approved` IS `I lived in Canada for the ten years just before the day my application is approved`
            `aggregate period of presence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, prior to those ten years` IS `years I was present in Canada after turning 18 and before those ten years`
            `aggregate periods of absence from Canada during those ten years` IS `years I was absent from Canada during those ten years`
            `resided in Canada for at least one year immediately preceding the day on which the person's application is approved` IS `I lived in Canada for at least one year just before the day my application is approved`
            `aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the person's application is approved` IS `years I have lived in Canada after turning 18 and before the day my application is approved`
            `was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which the person's application is approved` IS `I was living in Canada on the day before my application is approved`

-- s 3(2). A "partial monthly pension" is paid to a person who is 65, is not eligible for a full pension, and has lived in Canada after 18 for at least ten but
-- less than forty years (and, under twenty years, was living in Canada the day before approval).
@export Am I qualified for a partial monthly pension (s 3(2))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day my application is approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day is (or will) your application for the pension be approved? (If you are asking about now, give today's date.)
      `my application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had your application for an old age pension been approved by July 1, 1977?
      `I lived in Canada on July 1, 1977` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you live in Canada on July 1, 1977?
      `I had lived in Canada for any period after turning 18 before that` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you did not live in Canada on July 1, 1977: had you lived in Canada for any period after turning 18?
      `I held a valid immigration visa on July 1, 1977` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you hold a valid immigration visa on July 1, 1977?
      `I lived in Canada for the ten years just before the day my application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you live in Canada for the ten years immediately before the day your application is approved?
      `years I was present in Canada after turning 18 and before those ten years` IS A NUMBER @desc In total, how many years were you present in Canada after turning 18 and before those ten years? (0 if none)
      `years I was absent from Canada during those ten years` IS A NUMBER @desc In total, how many years were you absent from Canada during those ten years? (0 if none)
      `I lived in Canada for at least one year just before the day my application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you live in Canada for at least one year immediately before the day your application is approved?
      `years I have lived in Canada after turning 18 and before the day my application is approved` IS A NUMBER @desc In total, how many years have you lived in Canada after turning 18 and before the day your application is approved?
      `I was living in Canada on the day before my application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you living in Canada on the day before your application is approved?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(2): Am I qualified for a partial monthly pension` IF
    `s 3(2): a partial monthly pension may be paid to the person` `my age and residence facts`
    WHERE
        `my age and residence facts` MEANS `s 3: Facts of age and residence` WITH
            `the date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `the day on which the person's application is approved` IS `the day my application is approved`
            `the person's application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977` IS `my application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977`
            `resided in Canada on July 1, 1977` IS `I lived in Canada on July 1, 1977`
            `had resided in Canada for any period after attaining eighteen years of age` IS `I had lived in Canada for any period after turning 18 before that`
            `possessed a valid immigration visa on July 1, 1977` IS `I held a valid immigration visa on July 1, 1977`
            `resided in Canada for the ten years immediately preceding the day on which the person's application is approved` IS `I lived in Canada for the ten years just before the day my application is approved`
            `aggregate period of presence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, prior to those ten years` IS `years I was present in Canada after turning 18 and before those ten years`
            `aggregate periods of absence from Canada during those ten years` IS `years I was absent from Canada during those ten years`
            `resided in Canada for at least one year immediately preceding the day on which the person's application is approved` IS `I lived in Canada for at least one year just before the day my application is approved`
            `aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the person's application is approved` IS `years I have lived in Canada after turning 18 and before the day my application is approved`
            `was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which the person's application is approved` IS `I was living in Canada on the day before my application is approved`

-- s 4(1). A person who was not a pensioner on July 1, 1977 gets a pension only if, the day before approval, they are a Canadian citizen or legally resident,
-- or, the day before they ceased to live in Canada, they were. Whether you were "legally resident" is Regulations s 22 (not in this layer): state it as a fact.
@export Do I meet the requirement of legal residence for a pension (s 4(1))?
GIVEN `my application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had your application for an old age pension been approved by July 1, 1977?
      `I am a Canadian citizen on the day before my application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a Canadian citizen on the day before your application is approved?
      `I am legally resident in Canada on the day before my application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not a citizen: are you legally resident in Canada on the day before your application is approved?
      `I have ceased to live in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ceased to live in Canada?
      `I was a Canadian citizen on the day before I ceased to live in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a Canadian citizen on the day before you ceased to live in Canada?
      `I was legally resident in Canada on the day before I ceased to live in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not a citizen: were you legally resident in Canada on the day before you ceased to live in Canada?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4(1): Do I meet the requirement of legal residence for the pension` IF
    `s 4(1): the person meets the requirement of legal residence for a pension under this Part` `my citizenship and legal residence facts`
    WHERE
        `my citizenship and legal residence facts` MEANS `s 4(1): Facts of citizenship and legal residence` WITH
            `the person's application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977` IS `my application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977`
            `on the day preceding the day on which the person's application is approved, the person is a Canadian citizen` IS `I am a Canadian citizen on the day before my application is approved`
            `on the day preceding the day on which the person's application is approved, the person is legally resident in Canada` IS `I am legally resident in Canada on the day before my application is approved`
            `the person has ceased to reside in Canada` IS `I have ceased to live in Canada`
            `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada, the person was a Canadian citizen` IS `I was a Canadian citizen on the day before I ceased to live in Canada`
            `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada, the person was legally resident in Canada` IS `I was legally resident in Canada on the day before I ceased to live in Canada`

-- s 4.1(a). If the Minister intends to waive your need to apply (s 5(4)) and holds the prescribed information about you, you are presumed to meet the residence requirement,
-- unless there is evidence to the contrary. "Prescribed information" is Regulations (not in this layer): ask whether the Minister's information includes it.
@export If the Minister intends to waive my application, is my period-of-residence requirement treated as met (s 4.1(a))?
GIVEN `the Minister intends to waive the requirement that I apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister intend to waive the requirement that you apply for the pension?
      `the Minister's information about me includes the prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information the Minister already has about you include the information the regulations prescribe?
      `there is evidence that I do not meet the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence that you do not meet the residence requirement?
      `I actually meet the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you actually meet the residence requirement (ten years, or forty years, or ten to forty years, as s 3 states)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4.1(a): Is my residence requirement treated as met when the Minister intends to waive my application` IF
    `s 4.1(a): the requirement of subparagraph 3(1)(b)(iii) or (c)(iii) or paragraph 3(2)(b) is treated as met` `I actually meet the residence requirement` `I am presumed to meet it`
    WHERE
        `I am presumed to meet it` MEANS `s 4.1: the person is presumed to have met the requirements` (`s 4.1: the presumption applies` `the Minister intends to waive the requirement that I apply` `the Minister's information about me includes the prescribed information`) `there is evidence that I do not meet the requirement`

@export If the Minister intends to waive my application, is my legal-residence requirement treated as met (s 4.1(b))?
GIVEN `the Minister intends to waive the requirement that I apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister intend to waive the requirement that you apply for the pension?
      `the Minister's information about me includes the prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information the Minister already has about you include the information the regulations prescribe?
      `there is evidence that I do not meet the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence that you do not meet the legal-residence requirement?
      `I actually meet paragraph 4(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you actually meet the legal-residence requirement (citizen or legally resident the day before approval, or before you ceased to live in Canada)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4.1(b): Is my legal-residence requirement treated as met when the Minister intends to waive my application` IF
    `s 4.1(b): the requirement of paragraph 4(1)(a) or (b) is treated as met` `I actually meet paragraph 4(1)(a) or (b)` `I am presumed to meet it`
    WHERE
        `I am presumed to meet it` MEANS `s 4.1: the person is presumed to have met the requirements` (`s 4.1: the presumption applies` `the Minister intends to waive the requirement that I apply` `the Minister's information about me includes the prescribed information`) `there is evidence that I do not meet the requirement`

-- s 5(1). No pension is paid unless you are qualified under s 3(1) or (2), an application has been made by or for you, and it has been approved.
@export May a pension be paid to me (s 5(1))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day my application is approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day is (or will) your application for the pension be approved? (If you are asking about now, give today's date.)
      `my application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had your application for an old age pension been approved by July 1, 1977?
      `I lived in Canada on July 1, 1977` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you live in Canada on July 1, 1977?
      `I had lived in Canada for any period after turning 18 before that` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you did not live in Canada on July 1, 1977: had you lived in Canada for any period after turning 18?
      `I held a valid immigration visa on July 1, 1977` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you hold a valid immigration visa on July 1, 1977?
      `I lived in Canada for the ten years just before the day my application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you live in Canada for the ten years immediately before the day your application is approved?
      `years I was present in Canada after turning 18 and before those ten years` IS A NUMBER @desc In total, how many years were you present in Canada after turning 18 and before those ten years? (0 if none)
      `years I was absent from Canada during those ten years` IS A NUMBER @desc In total, how many years were you absent from Canada during those ten years? (0 if none)
      `I lived in Canada for at least one year just before the day my application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you live in Canada for at least one year immediately before the day your application is approved?
      `years I have lived in Canada after turning 18 and before the day my application is approved` IS A NUMBER @desc In total, how many years have you lived in Canada after turning 18 and before the day your application is approved?
      `I was living in Canada on the day before my application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you living in Canada on the day before your application is approved?
      `an application for a pension has been made by me or on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application for the pension been made by you or on your behalf?
      `my application has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your application been approved?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(1): May a pension be paid to me` IF
    `s 5(1): a pension may be paid to the person` `my age and residence facts` `an application for a pension has been made by me or on my behalf` `my application has been approved`
    WHERE
        `my age and residence facts` MEANS `s 3: Facts of age and residence` WITH
            `the date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `the day on which the person's application is approved` IS `the day my application is approved`
            `the person's application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977` IS `my application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977`
            `resided in Canada on July 1, 1977` IS `I lived in Canada on July 1, 1977`
            `had resided in Canada for any period after attaining eighteen years of age` IS `I had lived in Canada for any period after turning 18 before that`
            `possessed a valid immigration visa on July 1, 1977` IS `I held a valid immigration visa on July 1, 1977`
            `resided in Canada for the ten years immediately preceding the day on which the person's application is approved` IS `I lived in Canada for the ten years just before the day my application is approved`
            `aggregate period of presence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, prior to those ten years` IS `years I was present in Canada after turning 18 and before those ten years`
            `aggregate periods of absence from Canada during those ten years` IS `years I was absent from Canada during those ten years`
            `resided in Canada for at least one year immediately preceding the day on which the person's application is approved` IS `I lived in Canada for at least one year just before the day my application is approved`
            `aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the person's application is approved` IS `years I have lived in Canada after turning 18 and before the day my application is approved`
            `was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which the person's application is approved` IS `I was living in Canada on the day before my application is approved`

@export May a pension be paid to me for a particular day (s 5(1))?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask whether a pension may be paid?
      `the day my application is approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day is your application approved?
      `another provision of the Act allows payment for that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another provision of the Act allow a payment for a day before the day of approval (for example the earlier effective dates of s 8)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(1): May a pension be paid to me for a particular day` IF
    `s 5(1): a pension may be paid in respect of the day` `the day I ask about` `the day my application is approved` `another provision of the Act allows payment for that day`

@export Am I treated as having applied for, and been approved for, a pension when my allowance ends because I turn 65 (s 5(2))?
GIVEN `my allowance ceases to be payable because I reached 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your allowance ceased to be payable because you reached 65 years of age?
      `the Minister deems an application to have been made and approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister deem an application for the pension to have been made by you and approved, on the day you reached 65?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2): Am I treated as having applied when my allowance ends at 65` IF
    `s 5(2): the application is deemed to have been made and approved` `my allowance ceases to be payable because I reached 65` `the Minister deems an application to have been made and approved`

@export On what day did I reach 65 years of age, for the purposes of s 5(2)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 5(2): On what day did I reach 65` IS
    `s 5(2): the day on which the person reached sixty-five years of age` `my date of birth`

-- s 6. The Minister may obtain information about your age from census returns more than thirty years old, on the conditions the regulations set.
@export May the Minister obtain information about my age from Statistics Canada's census returns (s 6)?
GIVEN `the information is about the age of a pensioner or an applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information about the age of a pensioner or of an applicant for a pension?
      `the information is contained in the returns of a census` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information contained in the returns of a census?
      `the day the census was taken` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the census taken?
      `the day the Minister requests the information` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the Minister request the information?
      `the conditions in the regulations are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions specified in the regulations met?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6: May the Minister obtain my age from census returns` IF
    `s 6: the Minister is entitled to obtain the information from Statistics Canada on request` `the information is about the age of a pensioner or an applicant` `the information is contained in the returns of a census` `the day the census was taken` `the day the Minister requests the information` `the conditions in the regulations are met`

-- A group that arises only in a situation the person may not be in: a sentence of imprisonment. The form asks "Are you in prison?" before showing it.
§§ `Being in prison`

-- s 5(3). No pension is paid for a period in prison (after the first month of it) to a person serving a sentence (a) in a penitentiary or (b) of more than 90 days in a provincial prison
-- whose province has an agreement with the federal government. The Act's own "incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)" is this category.
@export Am I a person in prison for whom no pension may be paid (s 5(3))?
GIVEN `I am in prison` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in prison (serving a sentence of imprisonment)?
      `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your sentence to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament?
      `the length of my sentence in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days long is your sentence of imprisonment?
      `my sentence is to be served in a prison under the Prisons and Reformatories Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your sentence to be served in a prison, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and Reformatories Act?
      `my province has an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the government of the province where that prison is located made an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(3): Am I an incarcerated person for whom no pension may be paid` IF
    `s 5(3): the person is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` `I am in prison` `my sentence`
    WHERE
        `my sentence` MEANS `Sentence of imprisonment` WITH
            `to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary`
            `length in days` IS `the length of my sentence in days`
            `to be served in a prison as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and Reformatories Act` IS `my sentence is to be served in a prison under the Prisons and Reformatories Act`
            `the government of the province in which the prison is located has entered into an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act` IS `my province has an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act`

@export Is no pension payable to me for a given month because I am in prison (s 5(3))?
GIVEN `the month I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which month do you ask about? (Any day in it.)
      `I am in prison` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in prison (serving a sentence of imprisonment)?
      `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your sentence to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament?
      `the length of my sentence in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days long is your sentence of imprisonment?
      `my sentence is to be served in a prison under the Prisons and Reformatories Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your sentence to be served in a prison, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and Reformatories Act?
      `my province has an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the government of the province where that prison is located made an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act?
      `the day my imprisonment began` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your imprisonment begin?
      `I have been released` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been released?
      `the day I was released` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you released? (Any date if you have not been released.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(3): Is no pension payable to me for a month because I am in prison` IF
    `s 5(3): no pension may be paid for the month` `the month I ask about` (`s 5(3): the person is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` `I am in prison` `my sentence`) `the day my imprisonment began` `when I was released`
    WHERE
        `my sentence` MEANS `Sentence of imprisonment` WITH
            `to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary`
            `length in days` IS `the length of my sentence in days`
            `to be served in a prison as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and Reformatories Act` IS `my sentence is to be served in a prison under the Prisons and Reformatories Act`
            `the government of the province in which the prison is located has entered into an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act` IS `my province has an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act`
        `when I was released` MEANS IF `I have been released` THEN JUST `the day I was released` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 8(2.1). If your application is approved while you are in prison, payment starts for the month of your release, but only after you tell the Minister in writing (before or after release).
@export If my application is approved while I am in prison, in respect of which month does my pension start (s 8(2.1))?
GIVEN `my application is approved while I am in prison and described in subsection 5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application approved while you are in prison, serving a sentence that s 5(3) describes?
      `I have been released` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been released?
      `the day I was released` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you released? (Any date if you have not been released.)
      `I notify the Minister in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you notified the Minister in writing of your release (before or after it)?
      `the month in which payment would otherwise commence` IS A DATE @desc In which month would payment of your pension commence if you were not in prison? (Any day in it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 8(2.1): In respect of which month does my pension start if I am approved while in prison` IS
    `s 8(2.1): the month in respect of which payment of the pension commences` `my application is approved while I am in prison and described in subsection 5(3)` `when I was released` `I notify the Minister in writing` `the month in which payment would otherwise commence`
    WHERE
        `when I was released` MEANS IF `I have been released` THEN JUST `the day I was released` ELSE NOTHING

@export After prison, in respect of which month does my suspended pension resume (s 9.2)?
GIVEN `my pension is suspended because of my imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your pension suspended because of your imprisonment (s 5(3))?
      `I have been released` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been released?
      `the day I was released` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you released? (Any date if you have not been released.)
      `I notify the Minister in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you notified the Minister in writing (before or after your release)?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 9.2: In respect of which month does my suspended pension resume after prison` IS
    `s 9.2: the month in respect of which payment of the pension resumes` `my pension is suspended because of my imprisonment` `when I was released` `I notify the Minister in writing`
    WHERE
        `when I was released` MEANS IF `I have been released` THEN JUST `the day I was released` ELSE NOTHING

-- Questions about s 5(4) to (8): the Minister may waive the need to apply on your 65th birthday.
§§ `Applying, having my application waived, and withdrawing`

-- s 5(4). The Minister may, on the day you turn 65, waive the requirement that you apply, if satisfied from the information available that you are qualified for a pension.
@export May the Minister waive the requirement that I apply for a pension (s 5(4))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day the Minister waives the requirement` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the Minister waive the requirement that you apply?
      `the Minister is satisfied from the information available that I am qualified for the pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied, from the information available under the Act, that you are qualified for a pension under s 3(1) or (2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(4): May the Minister waive my need to apply` IF
    `s 5(4): the Minister may waive the requirement for an application` `my date of birth` `the day the Minister waives the requirement` `the Minister is satisfied from the information available that I am qualified for the pension`

@export Am I owed written notice, with the information the Minister relies on, of the intention to waive my application (s 5(5))?
GIVEN `the Minister intends to waive the requirement that I apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister intend to waive the requirement that you apply for a pension?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(5): Am I owed written notice of the Minister's intention to waive my application` IF
    `s 5(5): the person is owed written notice of the intention to waive, with the information on which the Minister intends to rely` `the Minister intends to waive the requirement that I apply`

-- s 5(6). You must file the statement before the day you turn 65: the last day is the day before your 65th birthday.
@export By what day must I file a statement correcting inaccuracies in the information the Minister gave me (s 5(6))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 5(6): By what day must I correct inaccuracies in the Minister's information` IS
    `s 5(6): the last day on which the person may file the statement correcting inaccuracies` `my date of birth`

@export Have I met my duty to file a statement correcting inaccuracies in the Minister's information (s 5(6))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the information the Minister gave me contains an inaccuracy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information the Minister gave you contain an inaccuracy?
      `I filed a statement correcting the inaccuracies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you filed with the Minister a statement correcting the inaccuracies?
      `the day I filed the statement` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you file it? (Any date if you have not.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(6): Have I met my duty to correct inaccuracies` IF
    `s 5(6): the person has complied` `my date of birth` `the information the Minister gave me contains an inaccuracy` `I filed a statement correcting the inaccuracies` `the day I filed the statement`

@export Have I declined the waiver of my application in time (s 5(7))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `I notified the Minister in writing that I decline the waiver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you notified the Minister in writing that you decline the waiver?
      `the day I notified the Minister` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you notify the Minister? (Any date if you have not.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(7): Have I declined the waiver in time` IF
    `s 5(7): the person has declined the waiver` `my date of birth` `I notified the Minister in writing that I decline the waiver` `the day I notified the Minister`

@export Am I required to make an application even though the Minister intended to waive it (s 5(8))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the Minister intended to waive the requirement that I apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister intend to waive the requirement that you apply?
      `the Minister requires me to make an application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister required you to make an application for the pension?
      `the day the Minister required it` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Minister require it?
      `the Minister notified me in writing of that requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister notify you in writing of that requirement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(8): Am I required to make an application despite the waiver` IF
    `s 5(8): the person is required to make an application` `my date of birth` `the Minister intended to waive the requirement that I apply` `the Minister requires me to make an application` `the day the Minister required it` `the Minister notified me in writing of that requirement`

@export Is the requirement that I apply for a pension waived for me (s 5(4) to (8))?
GIVEN `the Minister may waive the requirement that I apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does s 5(4) allow the Minister to waive the requirement in your case (see the question on s 5(4))?
      `I have declined the waiver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you declined the waiver in time?
      `I am required to make an application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister required you to make an application in time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(4): Is the requirement that I apply waived` IF
    `s 5(4): the requirement for an application is waived` `the Minister may waive the requirement that I apply` `I have declined the waiver` `I am required to make an application`

@export May I withdraw my application for a pension (s 5.1(1))?
GIVEN `I give the Minister a written notice of my withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the Minister a written notice withdrawing your application?
      `the day I give the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you give the notice?
      `the day payment of my pension commences` IS A DATE @desc On what day does payment of your pension commence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5.1(1): May I withdraw my application` IF
    `s 5.1(1): the applicant may withdraw the application` `I give the Minister a written notice of my withdrawal` `the day I give the notice` `the day payment of my pension commences`

@export After I withdraw, may my application still be used to decide whether I am eligible on a given day (s 5.1(2))?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `I withdrew my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you withdraw your application?
      `the day I withdrew my application` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you withdraw it? (Any date if you did not.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5.1(2): May my withdrawn application still be used` IF
    `s 5.1(2): the application may be used to determine the applicant's eligibility on the day` `the day I ask about` `my withdrawal`
    WHERE
        `my withdrawal` MEANS IF `I withdrew my application` THEN JUST `the day I withdrew my application` ELSE NOTHING

§ `How much pension, and when it is paid`

-- The full monthly pension is worked out by the Act from a figure for January to March 1985 and the quarterly adjustments (s 7); the person cannot state it, so the questions below ask for the published figure.
§§ `How much pension?`

-- s 3(3) and (4). A partial pension is the full pension times (your years of residence, rounded down to a whole year) over 40. The full pension in s 3(3) is the amount before any increase for putting off
-- your application (s 2.1(1)); the rule takes a second amount only to show which one the Act means, and ignores it, so the same figure is passed twice.
@export How much is my partial monthly pension for a month (s 3(3))?
GIVEN `the full monthly pension for the month, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the full monthly pension for the month you ask about, in dollars, as Service Canada publishes it?
      `years I have lived in Canada after turning 18 and before the day my application is approved` IS A NUMBER @desc In total, how many years (fractions allowed) have you lived in Canada after turning 18 and before the day your application is approved?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 3(3): How much is my partial monthly pension` IS
    `s 3(3): the amount of a partial monthly pension` `the full monthly pension for the month, in dollars` `the full monthly pension for the month, in dollars` `years I have lived in Canada after turning 18 and before the day my application is approved`

@export How many whole years of residence count towards my partial pension (s 3(4))?
GIVEN `years I have lived in Canada after turning 18 and before the day my application is approved` IS A NUMBER @desc In total, how many years (fractions allowed) have you lived in Canada after turning 18 and before the day your application is approved?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 3(4): How many whole years of residence count` IS
    `s 3(4): the aggregate period rounded to the lower multiple of a year` `years I have lived in Canada after turning 18 and before the day my application is approved`

@export May a later period of residence in Canada increase my partial pension (s 3(5))?
GIVEN `my application for a partial monthly pension has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your application for a partial monthly pension been approved?
      `the first day of the later period of residence` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the later period of residence in Canada begin?
      `the day my application was approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your application approved?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(5): May later residence increase my partial pension` IF
    `s 3(5): the amount of monthly pension payable may be increased on the basis of the period of residence` `my application for a partial monthly pension has been approved` `the first day of the later period of residence` `the day my application was approved`

@export What full monthly pension does the Act itself state for a given month (s 7(1))?
GIVEN `the month I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which month do you ask about? (Any day in it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 7(1): What does the Act itself say the full pension is for a month` IS
    `s 7(1): the amount of the full monthly pension stated for the month` `the month I ask about`

-- s 7(2) to (4). Each payment quarter after March 31, 1985 the pension is the previous quarter's amount times the ratio of two Consumer Price Index figures (s 7(2)), never less than before (s 7(3)),
-- and not adjusted after a fall until the index rises above its level at the fall (s 7(4)). The regulations (not in this layer) say how the index figures are averaged: ask for the averaged figures.
@export What is the full monthly pension for a payment quarter after the quarterly adjustment (ss 7(2) to (4))?
GIVEN `the first day of the payment quarter` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the payment quarter you ask about?
      `the full monthly pension in the three months before that quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the full monthly pension for a month in the three-month period before that quarter, in dollars?
      `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to that payment quarter (as the regulations average it)?
      `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to that payment quarter?
      `an earlier fall in the Consumer Price Index is holding the adjustment back` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an earlier fall in the Consumer Price Index still holding adjustments back (s 7(4)(b))?
      `the index carried forward from the earlier fall` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: what is the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter of the quarter in which the fall happened? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 7(2) to (4): What is the full monthly pension after the quarterly adjustment` IS
    CONSIDER `s 7(2) to (4): the quarterly adjustment` `the first day of the payment quarter` `the full monthly pension in the three months before that quarter` `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter` `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter` `the index carried forward, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST result THEN JUST (result's `the amount that may be paid for a month in the payment quarter`)
    WHERE
        `the index carried forward, if any` MEANS IF `an earlier fall in the Consumer Price Index is holding the adjustment back` THEN JUST `the index carried forward from the earlier fall` ELSE NOTHING

@export After a quarterly adjustment, which Consumer Price Index figure is carried forward because of an earlier fall (s 7(4)(b))?
GIVEN `the first day of the payment quarter` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the payment quarter you ask about?
      `the full monthly pension in the three months before that quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the full monthly pension for a month in the three-month period before that quarter, in dollars?
      `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to that payment quarter (as the regulations average it)?
      `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to that payment quarter?
      `an earlier fall in the Consumer Price Index is holding the adjustment back` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an earlier fall in the Consumer Price Index still holding adjustments back (s 7(4)(b))?
      `the index carried forward from the earlier fall` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: what is the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter of the quarter in which the fall happened? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 7(4)(b): Which index figure is carried forward after a fall` IS
    CONSIDER `s 7(2) to (4): the quarterly adjustment` `the first day of the payment quarter` `the full monthly pension in the three months before that quarter` `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter` `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter` `the index carried forward, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST result THEN result's `the Consumer Price Index carried forward under paragraph 7(4)(b)`
    WHERE
        `the index carried forward, if any` MEANS IF `an earlier fall in the Consumer Price Index is holding the adjustment back` THEN JUST `the index carried forward from the earlier fall` ELSE NOTHING

@export What is my monthly pension after the 10% increase for people 75 and older (s 7(5))?
GIVEN `the month I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which month do you ask about? (Any day in it.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `my full monthly pension before that increase, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your full monthly pension for that month before the 10% increase, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 7(5): What is my pension after the 10% increase at 75` IS
    `s 7(5): the amount increased by 10% for a person aged 75 or older` `the month I ask about` `my date of birth` `my full monthly pension before that increase, in dollars`

-- s 7.1(1), (2), (4). Each month you put off applying after you became qualified raises the pension by 0.6%, from the month after the month you became qualified to the month of approval,
-- but not for any month before July 2013, after the month you turn 70, or in which a pensioner's pension would not be paid or would be suspended.
@export For how many months is my pension increased because I put off applying (s 7.1(4))?
GIVEN `the day I became qualified for the pension` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you become qualified to receive the pension?
      `the day my application is approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day is your application approved?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the months in the period in which the pension would not have been paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those months fall in a period of imprisonment (s 5(3)) or absence (s 9(1) or (3)) in which a pensioner's pension would not be paid or would be suspended?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 7.1(4): For how many months is my pension increased for putting off my application` IS
    `s 7.1(4): the number of months for which the pension is increased` `the day I became qualified for the pension` `the day my application is approved` `my date of birth` `the months in the period in which the pension would not have been paid`

@export What is my full monthly pension after the increase for putting off my application (s 7.1(1))?
GIVEN `my full monthly pension without the increase for putting off, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your full monthly pension for the month before any increase for putting off your application, in dollars?
      `the number of months for which my pension is increased` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months is your pension increased (see the question on s 7.1(4))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 7.1(1): What is my full pension after the increase for putting off my application` IS
    `s 7.1(1): the amount of the full monthly pension as it is increased` `my full monthly pension without the increase for putting off, in dollars` `the number of months for which my pension is increased`

@export What is my partial monthly pension after the increase for putting off my application (s 7.1(2))?
GIVEN `my partial monthly pension when I became qualified, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your partial monthly pension, worked out under s 3(3), at the time you became qualified, in dollars?
      `the number of months for which my pension is increased` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months is your pension increased (see the question on s 7.1(4))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 7.1(2): What is my partial pension after the increase for putting off my application` IS
    `s 7.1(2): the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is increased` `my partial monthly pension when I became qualified, in dollars` `the number of months for which my pension is increased`

@export What is my full pension after both the increase for putting off my application and the 10% increase at 75 (s 7.1(5))?
GIVEN `the month I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which month do you ask about? (Any day in it.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `my full monthly pension as increased for putting off, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your full monthly pension for the month after the increase for putting off your application, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 7.1(5): What is my full pension, increased for putting off, after the 10% increase at 75` IS
    `s 7.1(5): the amount of the full monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (1) and increased by 10% at 75` `the month I ask about` `my date of birth` `my full monthly pension as increased for putting off, in dollars`

@export What is my partial pension after both the increase for putting off my application and the 10% increase at 75 (s 7.1(6))?
GIVEN `the month I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which month do you ask about? (Any day in it.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `my partial monthly pension as increased for putting off, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your partial monthly pension for the month after the increase for putting off your application, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 7.1(6): What is my partial pension, increased for putting off, after the 10% increase at 75` IS
    `s 7.1(6): the amount of the partial monthly pension as it is increased under subsection (2) and increased by 10% at 75` `the month I ask about` `my date of birth` `my partial monthly pension as increased for putting off, in dollars`

@export What monthly pension am I to receive, the greatest of the amounts the Act allows (s 7.1(3))?
GIVEN `I am qualified to receive a full monthly pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you qualified to receive a full monthly pension?
      `my full monthly pension as increased for putting off, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: what is your full monthly pension as increased for putting off your application, in dollars?
      `I am qualified to receive a partial monthly pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you qualified to receive a partial monthly pension?
      `my partial monthly pension as increased for putting off, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: what is your partial monthly pension as increased for putting off your application, in dollars?
      `my partial monthly pension when my application is approved, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: what is your partial monthly pension, worked out under s 3(3), at the time your application is approved, in dollars?
      `I decide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you decide to receive something other than the greatest amount?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 7.1(3): What monthly pension am I to receive` IS
    `s 7.1(3): the amount of monthly pension the person is to receive` `my full amount, if any` `my increased partial amount, if any` `my partial amount at approval, if any` `I decide otherwise`
    WHERE
        `my full amount, if any` MEANS IF `I am qualified to receive a full monthly pension` THEN JUST `my full monthly pension as increased for putting off, in dollars` ELSE NOTHING
        `my increased partial amount, if any` MEANS IF `I am qualified to receive a partial monthly pension` THEN JUST `my partial monthly pension as increased for putting off, in dollars` ELSE NOTHING
        `my partial amount at approval, if any` MEANS IF `I am qualified to receive a partial monthly pension` THEN JUST `my partial monthly pension when my application is approved, in dollars` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `When is my pension paid, suspended, stopped or cancelled?`

-- s 8(1) and (2). Your pension is normally approved as of the day of approval, but the regulations may let it take effect from an earlier day: not before the day your application was received
-- (s 8(1)), or, if you were already 65 before then, not before the later of one year before the day it was received and your 65th birthday (s 8(2)).
@export As of which day is the approval of my application effective (s 8(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day my application was received` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your application for the pension received?
      `the day my application is approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day is your application approved?
      `the regulations let my approval take effect from an earlier day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations let your approval take effect from an earlier day (Old Age Security Regulations, s 5)?
      `that earlier day` IS A DATE @desc From which earlier day? (Any date if there is none.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 8: As of which day is my approval effective` IS
    `s 8: the day as of which the approval is effective` `my date of birth` `the day my application was received` `the day my application is approved` `the earlier day, if any`
    WHERE
        `the earlier day, if any` MEANS IF `the regulations let my approval take effect from an earlier day` THEN JUST `that earlier day` ELSE NOTHING

@export In which month does payment of my pension commence (s 8(1))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day my application was received` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your application for the pension received?
      `the day my application is approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day is your application approved?
      `the regulations let my approval take effect from an earlier day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations let your approval take effect from an earlier day (Old Age Security Regulations, s 5)?
      `that earlier day` IS A DATE @desc From which earlier day? (Any date if there is none.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 8(1): In which month does my pension start` IS
    `s 8(1): the month in which payment of the pension commences` (`s 8: the day as of which the approval is effective` `my date of birth` `the day my application was received` `the day my application is approved` `the earlier day, if any`)
    WHERE
        `the earlier day, if any` MEANS IF `the regulations let my approval take effect from an earlier day` THEN JUST `that earlier day` ELSE NOTHING

@export Is my pension paid for a given month, given the day I die (s 8(3))?
GIVEN `the month I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which month do you ask about? (Any day in it.)
      `the pensioner has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the pensioner died?
      `the day the pensioner died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the pensioner die? (Any date if not.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8(3): Is my pension still paid for a month` IF
    `s 8(3): the pension is still paid for the month` `the month I ask about` `the day of death, if any`
    WHERE
        `the day of death, if any` MEANS IF `the pensioner has died` THEN JUST `the day the pensioner died` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 9(1) and (2). A pensioner who stays outside Canada for six consecutive months after becoming a pensioner (not counting the month of leaving) has the pension suspended from the seventh month,
-- and may have it resumed with the month of return; but not if they had lived in Canada at least twenty years after turning 18 when they left and establish it.
@export Is my pension suspended for a month because I am outside Canada (s 9(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `the month I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which month do you ask about? (Any day in it.)
      `the month I left Canada` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you leave Canada? (Any day in it.)
      `the month I became a pensioner` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you become a pensioner? (Any day in it.)
      `I have returned to Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you returned to Canada?
      `the month I returned to Canada` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you return? (Any date if not.)
      `I had lived in Canada for at least twenty years after turning 18 when I left` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had you lived in Canada for at least twenty years after turning 18 when you left Canada, and can you establish it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(1) and (2): Is my pension suspended because I am outside Canada` IF
    `s 9(1) and (2): payment of the pension for the month is suspended because of absence` (`s 9(1): the pensioner has been absent from Canada and payment for the month falls to be suspended` `the month I ask about` `the month I left Canada` `the month I became a pensioner` `my return, if any`) (`s 9(2): payment of the pension may be continued without suspension` `I had lived in Canada for at least twenty years after turning 18 when I left`)
    WHERE
        `my return, if any` MEANS IF `I have returned to Canada` THEN JUST `the month I returned to Canada` ELSE NOTHING

@export Is my pension suspended for a month because I ceased to live in Canada (s 9(3) and (4))?
GIVEN `the month I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which month do you ask about? (Any day in it.)
      `the month I ceased to live in Canada` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you cease to live in Canada? (Any day in it.)
      `I have resumed living in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you resumed living in Canada?
      `the month I resumed living in Canada` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you resume? (Any date if not.)
      `I had lived in Canada for at least twenty years after turning 18 when I ceased to live in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had you lived in Canada for at least twenty years after turning 18 when you ceased to live in Canada, and can you establish it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(3) and (4): Is my pension suspended because I ceased to live in Canada` IF
    `s 9(3) and (4): payment of the pension for the month is suspended because the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada` (`s 9(3): the pensioner has ceased to reside in Canada and payment for the month falls to be suspended` `the month I ask about` `the month I ceased to live in Canada` `my resumption, if any`) `I had lived in Canada for at least twenty years after turning 18 when I ceased to live in Canada`
    WHERE
        `my resumption, if any` MEANS IF `I have resumed living in Canada` THEN JUST `the month I resumed living in Canada` ELSE NOTHING

@export May my pension be suspended because I failed to comply with the Act or regulations (s 9(5))?
GIVEN `I fail to comply with a provision of the Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you failed to comply with a provision of the Act or the regulations?
      `the Minister decides to suspend payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister decide to suspend payment of your pension?
      `I have since complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you since complied with those provisions?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(5): May my pension be suspended because I did not comply` IF
    `s 9(5): payment of the pension is suspended for failure to comply` `I fail to comply with a provision of the Act or the regulations` `the Minister decides to suspend payment` `I have since complied`

@export On what day does my pension cease to be payable after I ask the Minister to stop it (s 9.1(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `I made a written request that my pension cease to be payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a written request to the Minister that your pension cease to be payable?
      `the Minister approved the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved the request?
      `the day the Minister approved the request` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Minister approve it? (Any date if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 9.1(2): On what day does my pension cease after I ask it to` IS
    `s 9.1(2): the last day on which the pension is payable` `I made a written request that my pension cease to be payable` `the day of approval, if any`
    WHERE
        `the day of approval, if any` MEANS IF `the Minister approved the request` THEN JUST `the day the Minister approved the request` ELSE NOTHING

@export May I have my stopped pension reinstated (s 9.1(3))?
GIVEN `my pension has ceased to be payable under subsection 9.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your pension ceased to be payable because you asked the Minister to stop it?
      `I make a written request to reinstate it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make a written request to the Minister that it be reinstated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9.1(3): May I have my pension reinstated` IF
    `s 9.1(3): the pensioner may have the pension reinstated on request` `my pension has ceased to be payable under subsection 9.1(2)` `I make a written request to reinstate it`

@export In which month does payment of my reinstated pension commence (s 9.1(4))?
GIVEN `the day the Minister receives my request` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the Minister receive your request for reinstatement?
      `I chose a month in the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you choose a month in the request?
      `the month I chose` IS A DATE @desc Which month did you choose? (Any day in it; any date if you chose none.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 9.1(4): In which month does my reinstated pension start` IS
    `s 9.1(4): the month in which payment of the reinstated pension commences` `the day the Minister receives my request` `the month I chose, if any`
    WHERE
        `the month I chose, if any` MEANS IF `I chose a month in the request` THEN JUST `the month I chose` ELSE NOTHING

@export Is my pension payable for a given month, after I asked the Minister to stop it and perhaps to reinstate it (s 9.1)?
GIVEN `the month I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which month do you ask about? (Any day in it.)
      `my pension has ceased to be payable under subsection 9.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your pension ceased to be payable because you asked the Minister to stop it?
      `the last day on which my pension was payable` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it last payable? (Any date if it has not ceased.)
      `my pension has been reinstated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your pension been reinstated?
      `the month my reinstated pension commences` IS A DATE @desc In which month does your reinstated pension commence? (Any date if not reinstated.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9.1: Is my pension payable for a month after I asked to stop it` IF
    `s 9.1: the pension has not ceased to be payable for the month` `the month I ask about` `my last payable day, if any` `my reinstatement month, if any`
    WHERE
        `my last payable day, if any` MEANS IF `my pension has ceased to be payable under subsection 9.1(2)` THEN JUST `the last day on which my pension was payable` ELSE NOTHING
        `my reinstatement month, if any` MEANS IF `my pension has been reinstated` THEN JUST `the month my reinstated pension commences` ELSE NOTHING

@export May I ask to cancel my pension (s 9.3(1))?
GIVEN `I make the request in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make the request in the prescribed manner?
      `the day payment of my pension commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what day did payment of your pension commence?
      `the day I make the request` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make the request?
      `the number of months after payment commenced within which the regulations let me ask` IS A NUMBER @desc Within how many months after payment commenced do the Old Age Security Regulations (s 26.1) let you ask? (They say six.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9.3(1): May I ask to cancel my pension` IF
    `s 9.3(1): the pensioner may request cancellation of the pension` `I make the request in the prescribed manner` `the day payment of my pension commenced` `the day I make the request` (`a limit in months` `the number of months after payment commenced within which the regulations let me ask`)

@export If I cancel, is my application treated as never made and the pension treated as not payable (s 9.3(2))?
GIVEN `my request is granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister granted your request?
      `the day my request is granted` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your request granted?
      `I have repaid the pension and any related supplement and allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you repaid the pension and any related supplement and allowance?
      `the day I repaid it` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you repay it? (Any date if not.)
      `the number of months after the request is granted within which the regulations require repayment` IS A NUMBER @desc Within how many months after the request is granted do the Old Age Security Regulations (s 26.1) require repayment? (They say six.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9.3(2): Is my application treated as never made after I cancel` IF
    `s 9.3(2): the application is deemed never to have been made and the pension is deemed not to have been payable` `my request is granted` `the day my request is granted` `my repayment day, if any` (`a limit in months` `the number of months after the request is granted within which the regulations require repayment`)
    WHERE
        `my repayment day, if any` MEANS IF `I have repaid the pension and any related supplement and allowance` THEN JUST `the day I repaid it` ELSE NOTHING

§ `Old Age Security Act, Part IV -- the questions about applying, appealing, being paid too much, and what the Minister may do`

§§ `Waiver, incapacity, death and error`

@export When the requirement that I apply is waived, on what day is my application deemed to have been made (s 26.1)?
GIVEN `the requirement that I apply has been waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister waived the requirement that you apply for a benefit?
      `the day the requirement was waived` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it waived?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 26.1: On what day is my application deemed made once the requirement is waived` IS
    `s 26.1: the day on which the application is deemed to have been made` `the requirement that I apply has been waived` `the day the requirement was waived`

-- s 26.1. Once the Minister waives your need to apply, your application is treated as made that day, and you cannot be paid for a month more than 11 months before the month of that day.
-- The answer here says only whether this limit stops you; whether the benefit is otherwise payable is another question.
@export Once my application is deemed made by a waiver, is a month before it barred because it is more than 11 months earlier (s 26.1)?
GIVEN `the month I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which month do you ask about? (Any day in it.)
      `the day my application is deemed to have been made` IS A DATE @desc On what day is your application deemed to have been made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 26.1: May I be paid for a month before the waiver` IF
    `s 26.1: the limit of 11 months before the month of the deemed application does not bar the benefit for the month` `the month I ask about` `the day my application is deemed to have been made`

@export May the Minister collect, share and use my personal information to invite people to apply for benefits (s 26.2)?
GIVEN `the purpose is to invite persons to make an application for benefits under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to invite persons to make an application for benefits under the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 26.2: May the Minister collect and use my information to invite people to apply` IF
    `s 26.2: the Minister may collect, make available or use personal information for the purpose` `the purpose is to invite persons to make an application for benefits under the Act`

-- s 28.1. If you could not form or express an intention to apply, the Minister may deem your application made earlier: in the later of the month before the first month the benefit could have been paid
-- and the month your last period of incapacity began. The Minister's satisfaction is an input, not a guess.
@export If an application was made on my behalf when I could not form an intention to apply, in which month may it be deemed made (s 28.1(1))?
GIVEN `the application was made on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the application made on your behalf?
      `the Minister is satisfied that I was incapable of forming or expressing an intention to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied, on the evidence, that you were incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application on the day it was actually made?
      `the first month in which the benefit could have commenced to be paid` IS A DATE @desc In which month could the benefit first have commenced to be paid? (Any day in it.)
      `the month the Minister considers my last period of incapacity to have commenced` IS A DATE @desc In which month does the Minister consider your last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced? (Any day in it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 28.1(1): In which month may my application made for me be deemed made` IS
    `s 28.1(1): the month in which the Minister may deem the application to have been made` `the application was made on my behalf` `the Minister is satisfied that I was incapable of forming or expressing an intention to apply` `the first month in which the benefit could have commenced to be paid` `the month the Minister considers my last period of incapacity to have commenced`

@export If I was incapable of applying, recovered, and then applied, in which month may my application be deemed made (s 28.1(2))?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that I was incapable of forming or expressing an intention to apply before the day I applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied, on the evidence, that you were incapable of forming or expressing an intention to apply before the day the application was actually made?
      `the day I ceased to be incapable` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you cease to be incapable?
      `the number of days of my incapacity` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days did your period of incapacity last?
      `the day my application was actually made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your application actually made?
      `the first month in which the benefit could have commenced to be paid` IS A DATE @desc In which month could the benefit first have commenced to be paid? (Any day in it.)
      `the month the Minister considers my last period of incapacity to have commenced` IS A DATE @desc In which month does the Minister consider your last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced? (Any day in it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 28.1(2): In which month may my late application be deemed made after my incapacity` IS
    `s 28.1(2): the month in which the Minister may deem the application to have been made` `the Minister is satisfied that I was incapable of forming or expressing an intention to apply before the day I applied` `the day I ceased to be incapable` `the number of days of my incapacity` `the day my application was actually made` `the first month in which the benefit could have commenced to be paid` `the month the Minister considers my last period of incapacity to have commenced`

@export Does my period of incapacity count for the purposes of s 28.1(1) and (2), being continuous (s 28.1(3))?
GIVEN `my period of incapacity was continuous` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your period of incapacity continuous?
      `the regulations otherwise prescribe for my period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations otherwise prescribe for your kind of period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28.1(3): Does my period of incapacity count` IF
    `s 28.1(3): the period of incapacity counts for the purposes of subsections (1) and (2)` `my period of incapacity was continuous` `the regulations otherwise prescribe for my period`

@export Does s 28.1 apply to me, having been incapacitated on or after January 1, 1995 (s 28.1(4))?
GIVEN `the latest day on which I was incapacitated` IS A DATE @desc What is the latest day on which you were incapacitated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28.1(4): Does s 28.1 apply to me` IF
    `s 28.1(4): section 28.1 applies to the person` `the latest day on which I was incapacitated`

@export May an application be made for the pension that would have been payable to a person who has died (s 29(1))?
GIVEN `the person who died would have been entitled on approval of an application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the person who died, before they died, have been entitled on approval of an application to the pension?
      `I am the estate, a liquidator, executor, administrator or heir, or a prescribed person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the estate or succession, the liquidator, executor or administrator of it, an heir of the person, or a person the regulations prescribe?
      `the day the person died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the person die?
      `the day I make the application` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make the application?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(1): May an application be made for the pension a person who died would have received` IF
    `s 29(1): an application may be made for the pension that would have been payable to the deceased person` `the person who died would have been entitled on approval of an application` `I am the estate, a liquidator, executor, administrator or heir, or a prescribed person` `the day the person died` `the day I make the application`

@export When an application is made for a deceased person's pension, may the pension be paid to a given person (s 29(2))?
GIVEN `an application is made under subsection 29(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made for the pension of the person who died?
      `the payee is the estate or succession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payee the estate or succession?
      `the payee is a person that the regulations prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payee a person the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(2): To whom is the pension paid when the estate applies` IF
    `s 29(2): the pension is to be paid to the payee` `an application is made under subsection 29(1)` `the payee` `the payee is a person that the regulations prescribe`
    WHERE
        `the payee` MEANS IF `the payee is the estate or succession` THEN Estate ELSE `Other person`

@export On what day is an application for a deceased person's pension deemed to have been received (s 29(3))?
GIVEN `an application is made under subsection 29(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made for the pension of the person who died?
      `the day the person died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the person die?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 29(3): On what day is that application deemed received` IS
    `s 29(3): the day on which the application is deemed to have been received` `an application is made under subsection 29(1)` `the day the person died`

@export May a survivor apply for an allowance under section 19 within one year after the other person's death (s 30(1))?
GIVEN `the survivor would have been entitled to an allowance under section 19 had they made a joint application before the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the survivor have been entitled to an allowance under section 19 had the survivor and the deceased person made a joint application before the death?
      `the day the person died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the person die?
      `the day the survivor applies` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the survivor apply?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(1): May the survivor apply for an allowance within a year of the death` IF
    `s 30(1): the survivor may make application for an allowance under section 19` `the survivor would have been entitled to an allowance under section 19 had they made a joint application before the death` `the day the person died` `the day the survivor applies`

@export On what day is the survivor's application considered to have been received (s 30(2))?
GIVEN `an application is made under subsection 30(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the survivor made an application under s 30(1)?
      `the day the person died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the person die?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 30(2): On what day is the survivor's application considered received` IS
    `s 30(2): the day on which the application is considered to have been received` `an application is made under subsection 30(1)` `the day the person died`

@export If I disappeared and the Minister issues a certificate of presumed death, on what day am I deemed to have died (s 31(1))?
GIVEN `I disappeared under circumstances that in the Minister's opinion raise beyond a reasonable doubt a presumption of death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the applicant or beneficiary disappear under circumstances that in the Minister's opinion raise beyond a reasonable doubt a presumption of death?
      `the Minister issues a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister issue a certificate?
      `the date of death stated in the certificate` IS A DATE @desc What date of death does the certificate state?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 31(1): On what day am I deemed to have died if the Minister certifies my death` IS
    `s 31(1): the day on which the applicant or beneficiary is deemed to have died` `I disappeared under circumstances that in the Minister's opinion raise beyond a reasonable doubt a presumption of death` `the Minister issues a certificate` `the date of death stated in the certificate`

@export If the Minister later issues a new certificate with a different date, on what day am I deemed to have died (s 31(2))?
GIVEN `the date of death stated in the first certificate` IS A DATE @desc What date of death does the first certificate state?
      `the Minister issued a new certificate with a different date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister issue a new certificate stating a different date?
      `the date of death stated in the new certificate` IS A DATE @desc What date of death does the new certificate state? (Any date if none.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 31(2): On what day am I deemed to have died after a new certificate` IS
    `s 31(2): the day on which the applicant or beneficiary is deemed to have died` `the date of death stated in the first certificate` `the new certificate's date, if any`
    WHERE
        `the new certificate's date, if any` MEANS IF `the Minister issued a new certificate with a different date` THEN JUST `the date of death stated in the new certificate` ELSE NOTHING

@export If I was presumed dead and the Minister is satisfied that I am alive, from which month are my benefits reinstated (s 31(3))?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that I am alive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied from new information or evidence that you are alive?
      `the date of my presumed death stated in the certificate` IS A DATE @desc What date of presumed death does the certificate state?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 31(3): From which month are my benefits reinstated if I turn out to be alive` IS
    `s 31(3): the month effective which the person's benefits are reinstated` `the Minister is satisfied that I am alive` `the date of my presumed death stated in the certificate`

@export Is the Minister bound by the issuing or revoking of a death certificate by another authority (s 31(4))?
GIVEN `a death certificate is issued or revoked by another authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has another authority (not the Minister) issued or revoked a death certificate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 31(4): Is the Minister bound by another authority's death certificate` IF
    `s 31(4): the Minister is bound by the issuance or revocation` `a death certificate is issued or revoked by another authority`

@export If I was denied a benefit through erroneous advice or administrative error, must the Minister take remedial action (s 32)?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that erroneous advice or administrative error denied me a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that, through erroneous advice or administrative error in administering the Act, you were denied a benefit, or part of a benefit, you were entitled to?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 32: Is the Minister to make good an administrative error` IF
    `s 32: the Minister shall take remedial action to place the person in the position the person would be in under this Act had the erroneous advice not been given or the administrative error not been made` `the Minister is satisfied that erroneous advice or administrative error denied me a benefit`

-- Questions that arise only after a decision: the form asks "Has the Minister decided something you disagree with?" before showing the group.
§§ `Reconsideration and appeal`

-- s 27.1(1). You may ask the Minister to reconsider a decision that no benefit may be paid to you, or about the amount, within ninety days after you are notified in writing, or any longer period the Minister allows
-- (before or after the ninety days run out). The circumstances in which the Minister may allow a longer period are Regulations s 29.1 (not in this layer): ask whether the Minister did.
@export May I ask the Minister to reconsider a decision about my benefit (s 27.1(1))?
GIVEN `I am dissatisfied with a decision that no benefit may be paid to me or about the amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you dissatisfied with a decision that no benefit may be paid to you, or about the amount of a benefit that may be paid to you?
      `the day I was notified in writing of the decision` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you notified in writing of the decision?
      `the day I make the request` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make the request?
      `the Minister allowed a longer period for my request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister allow a longer period for your request?
      `the last day of the longer period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the longer period the Minister allowed? (Any date if none.)
      `I make the request in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make the request in the prescribed form and manner (Old Age Security Regulations, ss 29 and 29.1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 27.1(1): May I ask the Minister to reconsider a decision` IF
    `s 27.1(1): the person may make a request to the Minister for a reconsideration of the decision or determination` `I am dissatisfied with a decision that no benefit may be paid to me or about the amount` (`s 27.1: the request is made within the time allowed` `the day I was notified in writing of the decision` `the day I make the request` `the longer period, if any`) `I make the request in the prescribed form and manner`
    WHERE
        `the longer period, if any` MEANS IF `the Minister allowed a longer period for my request` THEN JUST `the last day of the longer period` ELSE NOTHING

@export May I ask the Minister to reconsider a penalty assessed against me (s 27.1(1.1))?
GIVEN `a penalty has been assessed against me under section 44.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a penalty been assessed against you under s 44.1?
      `I am dissatisfied with the decision to impose the penalty or its amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you dissatisfied with the decision to impose the penalty, or with its amount?
      `the day I was notified in writing of the decision` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you notified in writing of the decision?
      `the day I make the request` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make the request?
      `the Minister allowed a longer period for my request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister allow a longer period for your request?
      `the last day of the longer period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the longer period the Minister allowed? (Any date if none.)
      `I make the request in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make the request in the prescribed form and manner (Old Age Security Regulations, ss 29 and 29.1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 27.1(1.1): May I ask the Minister to reconsider a penalty` IF
    `s 27.1(1.1): the person may request the Minister to reconsider the decision to impose a penalty or the amount of the penalty` `a penalty has been assessed against me under section 44.1` `I am dissatisfied with the decision to impose the penalty or its amount` (`s 27.1: the request is made within the time allowed` `the day I was notified in writing of the decision` `the day I make the request` `the longer period, if any`) `I make the request in the prescribed form and manner`
    WHERE
        `the longer period, if any` MEANS IF `the Minister allowed a longer period for my request` THEN JUST `the last day of the longer period` ELSE NOTHING

@export Has the Minister done what the Minister is required to do on my request for reconsideration (s 27.1(2))?
GIVEN `the Minister has received my request for reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister received your request for reconsideration?
      `the Minister reconsidered without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister reconsider the decision without delay?
      `the Minister notified me of the decision in writing without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister notify you in writing, without delay, of the decision?
      `the notice gave the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the notice give the reasons for the decision?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 27.1(2): Has the Minister done what the Minister must do on my request` IF
    `s 27.1(2): the Minister has done what the Minister is required to do on the request` `the Minister has received my request for reconsideration` `the Minister reconsidered without delay` `the Minister notified me of the decision in writing without delay` `the notice gave the reasons`

@export May I appeal the Minister's decision on reconsideration to the Social Security Tribunal (s 28(1))?
GIVEN `I am dissatisfied with a decision of the Minister made on reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you dissatisfied with a decision of the Minister made on reconsideration under s 27.1 (including a decision about further time to make a request)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28(1): May I appeal the Minister's decision to the Social Security Tribunal` IF
    `s 28(1): the person may appeal the decision to the Social Security Tribunal` `I am dissatisfied with a decision of the Minister made on reconsideration`

@export If I say the Minister got my income wrong, must that ground of my appeal be referred to the Tax Court of Canada (s 28(2))?
GIVEN `it is a ground of my appeal that the Minister's decision as to income was incorrectly made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a ground of your appeal that the Minister's decision about the income (or income from a particular source) of an applicant, beneficiary, or their spouse or common-law partner was incorrectly made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28(2): Must my income ground of appeal go to the Tax Court of Canada` IF
    `s 28(2): the appeal on that ground must be referred for decision to the Tax Court of Canada` `it is a ground of my appeal that the Minister's decision as to income was incorrectly made`

@export Is the Tax Court of Canada's decision on the income ground final and binding on my appeal (s 28(2))?
GIVEN `the income ground has been referred to the Tax Court of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the income ground been referred to the Tax Court of Canada?
      `the Federal Courts Act allows the decision to be departed from` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Federal Courts Act allow the decision to be departed from?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28(2): Is the Tax Court's decision on income final and binding` IF
    `s 28(2): the decision of the Tax Court of Canada is final and binding for all purposes of the appeal to the Social Security Tribunal` `the income ground has been referred to the Tax Court of Canada` `the Federal Courts Act allows the decision to be departed from`

@export After the Social Security Tribunal decides, until what day may the Minister stay payment of my benefit pending judicial review (s 28(3))?
GIVEN `the Social Security Tribunal has made a decision in respect of my benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Social Security Tribunal made a decision in respect of your benefit?
      `the day the period for applying for judicial review expires` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period for applying under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision expire?
      `Her Majesty has applied for judicial review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has Her Majesty applied for judicial review of the decision?
      `the month all proceedings were completed` IS A DATE @desc In which month were all proceedings in the judicial review completed? (Any date if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 28(3): Until when may the Minister stay payment of my benefit after the Tribunal decides` IS
    `s 28(3): the last day until which the Minister may stay payment of the benefit` `the Social Security Tribunal has made a decision in respect of my benefit` `the day the period for applying for judicial review expires` `the month of completion, if any`
    WHERE
        `the month of completion, if any` MEANS IF `Her Majesty has applied for judicial review` THEN JUST `the month all proceedings were completed` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Information, form and attendance`

-- s 33.1. Despite any other Act or law, three bodies may pass information about you to the Minister if it is necessary for administering this Act: the tax authority (a), the immigration and citizenship department (b)
-- and the Correctional Service (c, personal information only). You have no right to stop it; the questions say when it is allowed.
@export May the Minister of National Revenue make a report about me available to the Minister, despite any other law (s 33.1(a))?
GIVEN `the report is made available by the Minister of National Revenue or a person designated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the report made available by the Minister of National Revenue or a person that Minister designates?
      `it is made available to the Minister or a designated public officer of the Department of Employment and Social Development` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made available to the Minister, or to a public officer of the Department of Employment and Social Development that the Minister designates?
      `the report provides information available to the Minister of National Revenue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report provide information that is available to the Minister of National Revenue?
      `the information is necessary for the administration of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information necessary for the administration of the Old Age Security Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 33.1(a): May the tax authority give the Minister a report about me` IF
    `s 33.1(a): the report may be made available` `the report is made available by the Minister of National Revenue or a person designated` `it is made available to the Minister or a designated public officer of the Department of Employment and Social Development` `the report provides information available to the Minister of National Revenue` `the information is necessary for the administration of the Act`

@export May the Minister of Citizenship and Immigration or that Department's staff make information about me available to the Minister (s 33.1(b))?
GIVEN `the information is made available by the Minister of Citizenship and Immigration or an officer or employee of that Department` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information made available by the Minister of Citizenship and Immigration or an officer or employee of that Department?
      `it is made available to the Minister or a public officer of the Department of Employment and Social Development` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made available to the Minister or a public officer of the Department of Employment and Social Development?
      `it was obtained in the administration of the Citizenship Act or the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it obtained in the administration of the Citizenship Act or the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `the information is necessary for the administration of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information necessary for the administration of the Old Age Security Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 33.1(b): May the immigration department give the Minister information about me` IF
    `s 33.1(b): the information may be made available` `the information is made available by the Minister of Citizenship and Immigration or an officer or employee of that Department` `it is made available to the Minister or a public officer of the Department of Employment and Social Development` `it was obtained in the administration of the Citizenship Act or the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act` `the information is necessary for the administration of the Act`

@export May the Commissioner of Corrections or the Correctional Service's staff make personal information about me available to the Minister (s 33.1(c))?
GIVEN `the personal information is made available by the Commissioner of Corrections or a staff member of the Correctional Service of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the personal information made available by the Commissioner of Corrections or a staff member of the Correctional Service of Canada?
      `it is made available to the Minister or a public officer of the Department of Employment and Social Development` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made available to the Minister or a public officer of the Department of Employment and Social Development?
      `it was obtained in the administration of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it obtained in the administration of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act?
      `the information is necessary for the administration of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information necessary for the administration of the Old Age Security Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 33.1(c): May the Correctional Service give the Minister personal information about me` IF
    `s 33.1(c): the personal information may be made available` `the personal information is made available by the Commissioner of Corrections or a staff member of the Correctional Service of Canada` `it is made available to the Minister or a public officer of the Department of Employment and Social Development` `it was obtained in the administration of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` `the information is necessary for the administration of the Act`

@export Is my application, statement or notification made in the form the Minister requires (s 35)?
GIVEN `the Minister requires a form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister require a particular form for it?
      `I made or gave it in that form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make or give it in that form?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35: Is my application made in the form the Minister requires` IF
    `s 35: the application, statement or notification is made or given as required` `the Minister requires a form` `I made or gave it in that form`

@export Can the Minister require me to be at a place at a time to apply in person or give more information (s 35.1)?
GIVEN `the Minister requires me, or a group I am in, to be at a place at a time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister require you (or a group you are in) to be at a place at a time?
      `the place is suitable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place suitable?
      `the time is suitable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the time suitable?
      `the purpose is to make an application in person or to give additional information about one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to make an application for benefits in person, or to give additional information about an application?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35.1: Can the Minister require me to attend in person` IF
    `s 35.1: the person is required to be at the place at the time` `the Minister requires me, or a group I am in, to be at a place at a time` `the place is suitable` `the time is suitable` `the purpose is to make an application in person or to give additional information about one`

@export Does the Minister's officer or employee who takes my oath or affidavit have all the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits (s 38(1))?
GIVEN `the person is an officer or employee of Her Majesty authorized by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an officer or employee of Her Majesty whom the Minister has authorized for the purpose?
      `they take it in the course of their employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they take your oath, affidavit, declaration or affirmation in the course of their employment?
      `another Act of Parliament or of a legislature provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another Act of Parliament, or of a provincial legislature, provide otherwise?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 38(1): Does the officer I swear before have a commissioner's powers` IF
    `s 38(1): the person has all the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits with respect to the oath, affidavit, declaration or affirmation` `the person is an officer or employee of Her Majesty authorized by the Minister` `they take it in the course of their employment` `another Act of Parliament or of a legislature provides otherwise`

@export Will the Minister accept my oath, affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation given before a federal or provincial government employee (s 38(2))?
GIVEN `it was given to an officer or employee of a federal or provincial department` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it given before an officer or employee of a department in the federal public administration (Schedule I, IV or V to the Financial Administration Act) or of a department of the government of a province?
      `that officer or employee has all the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that officer or employee have all the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits?
      `it is given for the purposes of the administration of the Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it given for the purposes of administering the Old Age Security Act or its regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 38(2): Will the Minister accept my oath or affidavit sworn before a government employee` IF
    `s 38(2): the Minister may accept the oath, affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation` `it was given to an officer or employee of a federal or provincial department` `that officer or employee has all the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits` `it is given for the purposes of the administration of the Act or the regulations`

§§ `Benefits cannot be assigned or seized, and what happens if I am paid too much`

-- s 36(1), (1.1). Your benefit cannot be assigned, charged, attached, anticipated or given as security, and cannot be seized or executed against. (The Minister's deductions under 36(2), (3) and 37 are separate.)
@export Is a transaction purporting to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give my benefit as security void (s 36(1))?
GIVEN `the transaction purports to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give a benefit as security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the transaction purport to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give a benefit as security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 36(1): Is a transaction that assigns my benefit void` IF
    `s 36(1): the transaction is void` `the transaction purports to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give a benefit as security`

@export Is my benefit liable to seizure or execution, at law or in equity (s 36(1.1))?
GIVEN `seizure or execution is sought against my benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is seizure or execution sought against your benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 36(1.1): Can my benefit be seized` IF
    `s 36(1.1): the benefit is liable to the seizure or execution` `seizure or execution is sought against my benefit`

@export How much of my benefit may the Minister deduct and pay to a province or municipality that paid me assistance (s 36(2))?
GIVEN `a province or municipality paid me an advance or assistance that would not have been paid if my benefit had been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a provincial or municipal authority pay you an advance, assistance or welfare payment for a month that would not have been paid if your benefit had been paid for it?
      `a benefit has subsequently become payable for that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a benefit subsequently become payable (or payment of a benefit may be made) to you for that period?
      `the prescribed terms and conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the terms and conditions the regulations prescribe (Old Age Security Regulations, s 28.1) met?
      `the amount of the advance, assistance or welfare payment, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was the advance, assistance or welfare payment, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 36(2): How much may the Minister deduct from my benefit for a province or municipality` IS
    `s 36(2): the most the Minister may deduct from the benefit and pay to the provincial authority or municipal authority` `a province or municipality paid me an advance or assistance that would not have been paid if my benefit had been paid` `a benefit has subsequently become payable for that period` `the prescribed terms and conditions are met` `the amount of the advance, assistance or welfare payment, in dollars`

@export How much of my benefit may the Minister deduct and pay to the Department of Veterans Affairs (s 36(3))?
GIVEN `I received a benefit from Veterans Affairs that I would not have received if my benefit had been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive, for a month, a benefit under an Act administered by the Minister of Veterans Affairs that you would not have received if your benefit under this Act had been paid for that period?
      `a benefit has subsequently become payable for that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a benefit under this Act subsequently become payable (or payment may be made) to you for that period?
      `I consented in writing to the deduction on or before receiving it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you consent in writing, on or before receiving the Veterans Affairs benefit, to the deduction and payment by the Minister?
      `the amount of the benefit I received from Veterans Affairs, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was the benefit you received from the Department of Veterans Affairs, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 36(3): How much may the Minister deduct from my benefit for Veterans Affairs` IS
    `s 36(3): the most the Minister may deduct from the benefit and pay to the Department of Veterans Affairs` `I received a benefit from Veterans Affairs that I would not have received if my benefit had been paid` `a benefit has subsequently become payable for that period` `I consented in writing to the deduction on or before receiving it` `the amount of the benefit I received from Veterans Affairs, in dollars`

-- s 37(1). A person paid a benefit they were not entitled to, or more than they were entitled to, must return it "forthwith" (the Act gives no number of days).
@export How much must I return forthwith if I was paid a benefit I was not entitled to, or too much (s 37(1))?
GIVEN `the benefit payment I received, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much benefit payment did you receive or obtain, in dollars?
      `the benefit payment I was entitled to, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much were you entitled to, in dollars? (0 if nothing.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 37(1): How much must I return if I was paid too much` IS
    `s 37(1): the amount the person shall forthwith return` `the benefit payment I received, in dollars` `the benefit payment I was entitled to, in dollars`

@export How much do I owe Her Majesty as a debt for a benefit payment I should not have had (s 37(2))?
GIVEN `the benefit payment I received, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much benefit payment did you receive or obtain, in dollars?
      `the benefit payment I was entitled to, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much were you entitled to, in dollars? (0 if nothing.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 37(2): How much is the debt I owe the Crown for a payment` IS
    `s 37(2): the debt due to Her Majesty for a benefit payment` `the benefit payment I received, in dollars` `the benefit payment I was entitled to, in dollars`

@export Can the debt for a benefit payment be recovered on a given day, however long ago it arose (s 37(2))?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask whether the debt is recoverable?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 37(2): Can the Crown still recover the debt on a given day` IF
    `s 37(2): the debt is recoverable on the day` `the day I ask about`

-- s 37(2), (2.01), (2.02). A benefit payment you should not have had, interest payable under the Act, and a penalty under s 44.1 are each a debt due to Her Majesty.
-- (The debt of s 37(2.8) is owed by the person who was served with a notice under s 37(2.7) and did not pay, so it is not added here; it has its own question.) The first figure is the excess you already worked out (s 37(1)), so the rule is given 0 as the amount you were entitled to.
@export How much in total do I owe Her Majesty under this Act, adding the debts for payments, interest and penalties (s 37(2), (2.01) and (2.02))?
GIVEN `my debt for benefit payments, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you owe for benefit payments (s 37(2)), in dollars?
      `the interest payable under the Act, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much interest is payable under the Act, in dollars?
      `the penalties imposed on me under section 44.1, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much in penalties has been imposed on you under s 44.1, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 37: How much in total do I owe Her Majesty` IS
    `oa1: the total of a person's debts for a payment, interest and a penalty` (`s 37(2): the debt due to Her Majesty for a benefit payment` `my debt for benefit payments, in dollars` 0) (`s 37(2.01): the debt due to Her Majesty for interest` `the interest payable under the Act, in dollars`) (`s 37(2.02): the debt due to Her Majesty for a penalty` `the penalties imposed on me under section 44.1, in dollars`)

@export How much of an amount payable to me may the Minister deduct and keep against my debt (s 37(2.1))?
GIVEN `my debt, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your debt, in dollars?
      `the amount payable to me, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is payable to you (or your estate) under this Act or any other Act or program the Minister administers, in dollars?
      `the deduction is made in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the deduction made in the prescribed manner (Old Age Security Regulations, s 27: in an amount that does not cause undue hardship)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 37(2.1): How much may the Minister take out of what is payable to me` IS
    `s 37(2.1): the most that may be deducted and retained out of the amount payable` `my debt, in dollars` `the amount payable to me, in dollars` `the deduction is made in the prescribed manner`

@export May the Minister certify the part of my debt that has not been recovered on a given day (s 37(2.2))?
GIVEN `part of the debt has not been recovered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has part of the debt not been recovered?
      `in the Minister's opinion I am attempting to avoid payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Minister's opinion, are you attempting to avoid payment?
      `the day of the default` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you default?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 37(2.2): May the Minister certify my debt on a given day` IF
    `s 37(2.2): the Minister may certify the debt that has not been recovered on the day` `part of the debt has not been recovered` `in the Minister's opinion I am attempting to avoid payment` `the day of the default` `the day I ask about`

@export Registered in the Federal Court, what judgment debt does the Minister's certificate have the force of (s 37(2.3))?
GIVEN `the certificate is produced to the Federal Court and registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the certificate been produced to the Federal Court and registered?
      `the amount specified in the certificate, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount does the certificate specify, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 37(2.3): What is a registered certificate worth` IS
    `s 37(2.3): the amount of the judgment debt that the certificate has the force and effect of` `the certificate is produced to the Federal Court and registered` `the amount specified in the certificate, in dollars`

@export May the registered certificate also be registered in the superior court of a province (s 37(2.4))?
GIVEN `the certificate has been registered in the Federal Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the certificate been registered in the Federal Court under s 37(2.3)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 37(2.4): May the certificate also be registered in a provincial superior court` IF
    `s 37(2.4): the certificate may also be registered in the superior court of a province` `the certificate has been registered in the Federal Court`

@export What costs and charges for registering the certificate can be recovered from me (s 37(2.5))?
GIVEN `the certificate has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the certificate been registered?
      `the reasonable costs and charges of registration, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the reasonable costs and charges for registering the certificate, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 37(2.5): What costs of registering the certificate can be recovered from me` IS
    `s 37(2.5): the costs and charges that are recoverable in the same way` `the certificate has been registered` `the reasonable costs and charges of registration, in dollars`

@export May a registered certificate be recorded as security, a charge, lien or legal hypothec on land I own in a province (s 37(2.6))?
GIVEN `a court document evidences a certificate registered against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a document issued by the Federal Court or a provincial superior court evidence a certificate registered against you?
      `the land or interest in land is in a province and is held or owned by me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the land (or interest in land) in a province and held or owned by you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 37(2.6): May a charge on my land be recorded for the debt` IF
    `s 37(2.6): the document may be recorded to create security, or a charge, lien or legal hypothec, on the land` `a court document evidences a certificate registered against me` `the land or interest in land is in a province and is held or owned by me`

@export May the Minister require a person who owes me money, or is about to, to pay it to the Receiver General (s 37(2.7))?
GIVEN `the Minister knows or suspects that a person is or is about to become indebted to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister know or suspect that a person is, or is about to become, indebted or liable to make a payment to you, when you are liable to make a payment to Her Majesty under this Act?
      `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice served personally or by confirmed delivery service?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 37(2.7): May the Minister require someone who owes me money to pay it to the Crown` IF
    `s 37(2.7): the Minister may require the first person to pay the money otherwise payable to the second person to the Receiver General` `the Minister knows or suspects that a person is or is about to become indebted to me` `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service`

@export How much is the debt to Her Majesty for an amount that was not paid as a notice under s 37(2.7) required (s 37(2.8))?
GIVEN `the amount not paid as the notice required, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was not paid as the notice required, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 37(2.8): How much is the debt for an amount not paid as a notice required` IS
    `s 37(2.8): the debt due to Her Majesty for an amount not paid as the notice requires` `the amount not paid as the notice required, in dollars`

@export Is an affidavit of the person who served me evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand (s 37(2.9))?
GIVEN `the Act or the regulations provide for personal service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act or the regulations provide for personal service of the request, notice or demand?
      `the affidavit states that the person has charge of the records and knowledge of the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state that the person has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts?
      `the affidavit states that the request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the request, notice or demand was served personally, on a named day, on the person it was directed to?
      `a true copy is attached as an exhibit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person identify a true copy of the request, notice or demand as an exhibit attached to the affidavit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 37(2.9): Is an affidavit evidence that I was served personally` IF
    `s 37(2.9): the affidavit is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand` `the Act or the regulations provide for personal service` `the affidavit states that the person has charge of the records and knowledge of the facts` `the affidavit states that the request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day` `a true copy is attached as an exhibit`

@export May the Minister remit all or part of what I owe for a benefit payment (s 37(4))?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied it cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the amount cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future?
      `the Minister is satisfied the costs of collecting are likely to equal or exceed the amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the administrative costs of collecting are likely to equal or exceed the amount to be collected?
      `the Minister is satisfied that repayment would cause me undue hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that repayment would cause you undue hardship?
      `the Minister is satisfied the amount is the result of erroneous advice or administrative error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the amount is the result of erroneous advice or administrative error in administering the Act?
      `I have been convicted of an offence in connection with obtaining the payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of an offence under the Act or the Criminal Code in connection with obtaining the payment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 37(4): May the Minister forgive what I owe` IF
    `s 37(4): the Minister may remit all or any portion of the amount or excess of the benefit payment` `the Minister is satisfied it cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future` `the Minister is satisfied the costs of collecting are likely to equal or exceed the amount` `the Minister is satisfied that repayment would cause me undue hardship` `the Minister is satisfied the amount is the result of erroneous advice or administrative error` `I have been convicted of an offence in connection with obtaining the payment`

@export Does section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act apply to amounts I owe Her Majesty under this Act (s 37(5))?
GIVEN `the amount is owing to Her Majesty under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount owing to Her Majesty under the Old Age Security Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 37(5): Does section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act apply to what I owe` IF
    `s 37(5): section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act applies in relation to the amount` `the amount is owing to Her Majesty under this Act`

-- A group that arises only if something has gone wrong: the form asks "Did you give false information, or fail to declare income or return a payment?" before showing it.
§§ `What can be done to me if I give false information or do not comply`

-- s 44(1). It is an offence, punishable on summary conviction, to knowingly make a false or misleading statement in an application or statement, to make one that is false or misleading through non-disclosure,
-- to obtain a payment by false pretences, or, as payee, to negotiate or try to negotiate a cheque you are not entitled to. Reading note: "knowingly" is taken to govern only the first of the three limbs (NOTES.md, fork).
@export Have I committed an offence by making a false or misleading statement, or by negotiating a cheque that is not mine (s 44(1))?
GIVEN `I knowingly made a false or misleading statement in an application or statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly make a false or misleading statement in an application or statement required or permitted by the Act?
      `I made an application or statement that is false or misleading because I did not disclose facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an application or statement that is false or misleading because facts were not disclosed?
      `I obtained a benefit payment by false pretences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain a benefit payment by false pretences?
      `I am the payee of a cheque` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the payee of a cheque?
      `I negotiated or tried to negotiate the cheque` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you negotiate or attempt to negotiate it?
      `I am not entitled to the cheque` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not entitled to it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44(1): Have I committed an offence` IF
    `s 44(1): the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` (`s 44(1)(a): the person has done an act described in paragraph (a)` `I knowingly made a false or misleading statement in an application or statement` `I made an application or statement that is false or misleading because I did not disclose facts` `I obtained a benefit payment by false pretences`) (`s 44(1)(b): the person has done an act described in paragraph (b)` `I am the payee of a cheque` `I negotiated or tried to negotiate the cheque` `I am not entitled to the cheque`)

@export What is the most I can be fined for the offence under s 44(1)?
GIVEN `I am guilty of the offence under s 44(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you guilty of the offence under s 44(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 44(1): What is the most I can be fined for the offence` IS
    `s 44(1): the greatest fine that this Act sets for the offence` `I am guilty of the offence under s 44(1)`

@export Is the information or complaint against me open to objection because it is for more than one matter or relates to more than one offence (s 44(2))?
GIVEN `the information or complaint is for more than one matter or relates to more than one offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information or complaint for more than one matter of complaint, or does it relate to more than one offence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44(2): Can the charge against me be challenged because it joins several matters` IF
    `s 44(2): the information or complaint is open to objection` `the information or complaint is for more than one matter or relates to more than one offence`

@export May proceedings against me for an offence be commenced on a given day (s 44(3))?
GIVEN `the day the Minister became aware of the subject-matter` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Minister become aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings?
      `the day proceedings are commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what day are proceedings commenced?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44(3): By when must proceedings against me begin` IF
    `s 44(3): proceedings in respect of an offence may be commenced on the day` `the day the Minister became aware of the subject-matter` `the day proceedings are commenced`

@export May I be prosecuted under s 44 or the Criminal Code for an act for which a penalty has been imposed on me under s 44.1 (s 44(4))?
GIVEN `a penalty for the act or omission has been imposed on me under section 44.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a penalty for the act or omission been imposed on you under s 44.1?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44(4): May I be prosecuted if a penalty was imposed for the same act` IF
    `s 44(4): a proceeding may be commenced under this section or the Criminal Code for the act or omission` `a penalty for the act or omission has been imposed on me under section 44.1`

-- s 44.1(1). Instead of prosecuting, the Minister may impose a penalty if the Minister becomes aware of facts that in the Minister's opinion establish that you (a) knowingly made a false or misleading statement, (a.1) knowingly failed to correct
-- inaccuracies in the Minister's information, (b) did so through non-disclosure, (c) knowingly failed to declare income, (d) received a payment you knew you were not entitled to and did not return it without delay, or (e) took part in any of those.
@export Can the Minister impose a penalty on me for something I did or failed to do (s 44.1(1))?
GIVEN `the Minister becomes aware of facts that in the Minister's opinion establish that I did one of these things` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister become aware of facts that in the Minister's opinion establish that you did one of the following?
      `I made a statement or declaration that I knew was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a statement or declaration, in an application or otherwise, that you knew was false or misleading?
      `I knowingly failed to correct inaccuracies in the Minister's information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly fail to correct inaccuracies in the information the Minister provided, as ss 5(6), 11(3.3), 15(2.4), 19(4.05) or 21(4.3) require?
      `I made a statement or declaration that I knew was false or misleading because of non-disclosure of facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a statement or declaration that you knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts?
      `I knowingly failed to declare my income to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly fail to declare to the Minister all or some of your income?
      `I received a benefit payment I knew I was not entitled to and did not return it without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive a benefit payment (or an excess) that you knew you were not entitled to and not return it without delay?
      `I participated in, assented to or acquiesced in one of those acts or omissions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you participate in, assent to or acquiesce in any of those acts or omissions?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.1(1): Can the Minister impose a penalty on me` IF
    `s 44.1(1): the Minister may impose a penalty on the person` `the Minister becomes aware of facts that in the Minister's opinion establish that I did one of these things` `my acts and omissions`
    WHERE
        `my acts and omissions` MEANS `s 44.1(1): Facts about the person's acts or omissions` WITH
            `made a statement or declaration in an application or otherwise that the person knew was false or misleading` IS `I made a statement or declaration that I knew was false or misleading`
            `knowingly failed to correct any inaccuracies in the information provided by the Minister as required by subsection 5(6), 11(3.3), 15(2.4), 19(4.05) or 21(4.3)` IS `I knowingly failed to correct inaccuracies in the Minister's information`
            `made a statement or declaration in an application or otherwise that the person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts` IS `I made a statement or declaration that I knew was false or misleading because of non-disclosure of facts`
            `knowingly failed to declare to the Minister all or some of the person's income` IS `I knowingly failed to declare my income to the Minister`
            `received or obtained by cheque or otherwise a benefit payment to which the person knew that they were not entitled, or a benefit payment that the person knew was in excess of the amount of the benefit payment to which they were entitled, and did not return the cheque or the amount of the benefit payment, or the excess amount, without delay` IS `I received a benefit payment I knew I was not entitled to and did not return it without delay`
            `participated in, assented to or acquiesced in an act or omission mentioned in any of paragraphs (a) to (d)` IS `I participated in, assented to or acquiesced in one of those acts or omissions`

@export What is the most the Minister can set my penalty at for each act or omission (s 44.1(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 44.1(2): What is the most the penalty can be` IS
    `s 44.1(2): the greatest amount of the penalty for each act or omission`

@export May the Minister set my penalty at a given amount (s 44.1(2))?
GIVEN `the amount of the penalty, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the penalty, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.1(2): May the Minister set my penalty at this amount` IF
    `s 44.1(2): the Minister may set the amount of the penalty at the amount` `the amount of the penalty, in dollars`

@export May a penalty be imposed on me on a given day (s 44.1(3))?
GIVEN `a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a prosecution for the act or omission been initiated against you?
      `the day the Minister became aware of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Minister become aware of the act or omission?
      `the day the penalty is imposed` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the penalty imposed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.1(3): Is it too late for the Minister to penalise me` IF
    `s 44.1(3): a penalty may be imposed on the person on the day` `a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against me` `the day the Minister became aware of the act or omission` `the day the penalty is imposed`

@export May the Minister rescind or reduce a penalty imposed on me (s 44.1(4))?
GIVEN `new facts are presented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are new facts presented?
      `the Minister is satisfied the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or by mistake as to, a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact?
      `the Minister is satisfied the penalty cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the penalty cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future?
      `the Minister is satisfied that payment would cause me undue hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that payment of the penalty would cause you undue hardship?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.1(4): May the Minister rescind or reduce my penalty` IF
    `s 44.1(4): the Minister may rescind the imposition of the penalty or reduce it` `new facts are presented` `the Minister is satisfied the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or by mistake as to, a material fact` `the Minister is satisfied the penalty cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future` `the Minister is satisfied that payment would cause me undue hardship`

@export What is the purpose of an administrative penalty under s 44.1 (s 44.1(1.1))?
GIVEN `a penalty has been imposed on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a penalty been imposed on you?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `s 44.1(1.1): What is the penalty for` IS
    `s 44.1(1.1): the purpose of the penalty`

-- A group that arises only if the Minister seeks to examine documents, enter premises, or require information from you.
§§ `If the Minister wants to inspect documents or enter my home`

@export May the Minister examine a document that relates to my entitlement to a benefit (s 44.2(2))?
GIVEN `the time is a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a reasonable time?
      `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the purpose relate to the administration or enforcement of the Act?
      `the document relates or may relate to a person's entitlement to a benefit or its amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document relate, or may it relate, to a person's entitlement to a benefit or the amount of a benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.2(2): May the Minister examine my documents` IF
    `s 44.2(2): the Minister may examine the document` `the time is a reasonable time` `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of the Act` `the document relates or may relate to a person's entitlement to a benefit or its amount`

@export May the Minister enter my premises, and my home only with my consent or a warrant (s 44.2(3))?
GIVEN `the premises or place is a dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place a dwelling-house (the whole or a part of a building or structure kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence, and certain connected buildings and mobile homes)?
      `the occupant consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the occupant consent to the Minister entering?
      `the Minister has a warrant issued by a judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister have a warrant issued by a judge under s 44.2(4)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.2(3): May the Minister enter my home without my consent` IF
    `s 44.2(3): the Minister may enter the premises or place` `the premises or place is a dwelling-house` `the occupant consents` `the Minister has a warrant issued by a judge`

@export May the Minister enter a place where the Minister believes a document about a benefit is or should be kept (s 44.2(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the Minister believes a document about a benefit is or should be kept there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister believe a document relating to the entitlement of a person to a benefit, or its amount, is or should be kept there?
      `s 44.2(3) permits the Minister to enter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does s 44.2(3) permit entry (not a dwelling-house, or consent, or a warrant)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.2(2)(a): May the Minister enter this place to look for documents` IF
    `s 44.2(2)(a): the Minister may enter the premises or place` `the Minister believes a document about a benefit is or should be kept there` `s 44.2(3) permits the Minister to enter`

@export Must I give the Minister all reasonable assistance, answer all proper questions and attend with the Minister at the premises (s 44.2(2)(b))?
GIVEN `I am the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place?
      `the Minister is examining a document or entering under s 44.2(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister examining a document or entering the premises under s 44.2(2)?
      `the questions relate to the administration or enforcement of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the questions relate to the administration or enforcement of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.2(2)(b): Must I help and answer the Minister's questions` IF
    `s 44.2(2)(b): the Minister may require the person to give all reasonable assistance, answer all proper questions and attend at the premises or place with the Minister` `I am the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place` `the Minister is examining a document or entering under s 44.2(2)` `the questions relate to the administration or enforcement of the Act`

@export May a judge issue a warrant allowing the Minister to enter my home (s 44.2(4))?
GIVEN `the Minister applies to the judge without notice to me (ex parte)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister apply to a judge without notice to you (ex parte)?
      `the judge is satisfied on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe my home is a place referred to in s 44.2(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe your home is a premises or place referred to in s 44.2(2)?
      `the judge is satisfied on oath that entry is necessary for administering or enforcing the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied by information on oath that entry is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of the Act?
      `the judge is satisfied on oath that entry has been refused or will probably be refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied by information on oath that entry has been refused, or that there are reasonable grounds to believe it will be refused?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.2(4): May a judge issue a warrant to enter my home` IF
    `s 44.2(4): a judge may issue a warrant authorizing the Minister to enter the dwelling-house` `the Minister applies to the judge without notice to me (ex parte)` `the judge is satisfied on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe my home is a place referred to in s 44.2(2)` `the judge is satisfied on oath that entry is necessary for administering or enforcing the Act` `the judge is satisfied on oath that entry has been refused or will probably be refused`

@export May a judge order me to give the Minister reasonable access to a document in my home (s 44.2(5))?
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that entry is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that entry into your home is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of the Act?
      `the judge is satisfied that access to a document has been or may be refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that access to a document that is or should be kept in your home has been, or may be expected to be, refused?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.2(5): May a judge order me to give access to a document` IF
    `s 44.2(5): the judge may order the occupant to provide the Minister with reasonable access to the document and make any other appropriate order` `the judge is satisfied that entry is necessary` `the judge is satisfied that access to a document has been or may be refused`

@export Can the Minister require me to provide information or a document by notice (s 44.2(6) and (7))?
GIVEN `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice served on you personally or by confirmed delivery service?
      `the notice stipulates a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice stipulate a reasonable time within which to provide it?
      `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the purpose relate to the administration or enforcement of the Act?
      `the requirement is about unnamed persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement to provide information or a document about one or more unnamed persons?
      `the Minister first obtained a judge's authorization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister first obtain the authorization of a judge (s 44.2(8))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.2(6): Must I provide the information or document the Minister asks for` IF
    `s 44.2(6): the Minister may require the person to provide the information, additional information or document` `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service` `the notice stipulates a reasonable time` `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of the Act` (`s 44.2(7): the Minister may impose the requirement on the third party` `the requirement is about unnamed persons` `the Minister first obtained a judge's authorization`)

@export May a judge authorize the Minister to require me, as a third party, to provide information about unnamed persons (s 44.2(8))?
GIVEN `the Minister applies to the judge without notice to me (ex parte)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister apply to a judge without notice (ex parte)?
      `the judge is satisfied on oath that the person or group is ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied by information on oath that the person or group is ascertainable?
      `the judge is satisfied on oath that the requirement is made to verify compliance with a duty under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied by information on oath that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under this Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.2(8): May a judge authorize a requirement about unnamed persons` IF
    `s 44.2(8): a judge may authorize the Minister to impose on a third party a requirement relating to one or more unnamed persons` `the Minister applies to the judge without notice to me (ex parte)` `the judge is satisfied on oath that the person or group is ascertainable` `the judge is satisfied on oath that the requirement is made to verify compliance with a duty under the Act`

@export Was the judge's authorization served with the notice as required (s 44.2(9))?
GIVEN `an authorization was granted under s 44.2(8)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an authorization granted under s 44.2(8)?
      `it was served together with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it served together with the notice?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.2(9): Must the authorization be served with the notice` IF
    `s 44.2(9): the authorization has been served as the Act requires` `an authorization was granted under s 44.2(8)` `it was served together with the notice`

@export May I, as a third party, apply for a review of the authorization on a given day (s 44.2(10))?
GIVEN `the day the notice was served on me` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice served on you?
      `the day I apply for the review` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you apply for the review?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.2(10): By when may I ask a judge to review the authorization` IF
    `s 44.2(10): the third party may apply for a review of the authorization on the day` `the day the notice was served on me` `the day I apply for the review`

@export On review, may the judge cancel the authorization (s 44.2(11))?
GIVEN `the judge is no longer satisfied that the conditions in s 44.2(8) are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge no longer satisfied that the conditions for the authorization in s 44.2(8) are met?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.2(11): May the judge cancel the authorization on review` IF
    `s 44.2(11): the judge may cancel the authorization previously granted` `the judge is no longer satisfied that the conditions in s 44.2(8) are met`

@export On review, may the judge confirm or vary the authorization (s 44.2(11))?
GIVEN `the judge is no longer satisfied that the conditions in s 44.2(8) are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge no longer satisfied that the conditions for the authorization in s 44.2(8) are met?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.2(11): May the judge confirm or vary the authorization on review` IF
    `s 44.2(11): the judge may confirm or vary the authorization` `the judge is no longer satisfied that the conditions in s 44.2(8) are met`

@export Is a certified copy of a document the Minister inspected evidence of the original, with the same probative force (s 44.2(12))?
GIVEN `the document was inspected, examined or provided in accordance with s 44.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the document inspected, examined or provided in accordance with s 44.2?
      `the copy was made by the person who inspected it or to whom it was provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the copy made, or caused to be made, by the person who inspected or examined it or to whom it was provided?
      `the copy is certified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy certified?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.2(12): Is a certified copy of my document evidence` IF
    `s 44.2(12): the copy is evidence of the nature and content of the original document and has the same probative force as the original` `the document was inspected, examined or provided in accordance with s 44.2` `the copy was made by the person who inspected it or to whom it was provided` `the copy is certified`

@export Have I contravened the prohibition on interfering with a person doing what s 44.2 authorizes (s 44.2(13))?
GIVEN `the other person is doing something s 44.2 authorizes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person doing something that s 44.2 authorizes?
      `I interfere with them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you interfere with them?
      `I prevent or attempt to prevent them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you prevent or attempt to prevent them from doing it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44.2(13): Have I broken the rule against interfering` IF
    `s 44.2(13): the person has contravened the prohibition` `the other person is doing something s 44.2 authorizes` `I interfere with them` `I prevent or attempt to prevent them`

@export What is the most I can be fined for interfering with a person doing what s 44.2 authorizes (s 44.2(13))?
GIVEN `I have contravened s 44.2(13)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you contravened s 44.2(13)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 44.2(13): What is the most I can be fined for interfering` IS
    `s 44.2(13): the greatest fine that this Act sets for the contravention` `I have contravened s 44.2(13)`

-- Groups that arise only where an international agreement applies to the person, or where a transitional provision names them.
§§ `Agreements with other countries and the transitional provisions`

@export Does a social security agreement with another country have the force of law in Canada on a given day (s 41(1))?
GIVEN `the day the order declaring the agreement in force comes into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the order declaring the agreement in force come into force?
      `the agreement has ceased to be in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the agreement ceased to be in force by its terms?
      `the day the agreement ceases to be in force` IS A DATE @desc On what day does it cease to be in force? (Any date if it has not.)
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 41(1): Does an agreement with another country have the force of law in Canada on a day` IF
    `s 41(1): the agreement has the force of law in Canada on the day` `the day the order declaring the agreement in force comes into force` `the day the agreement ceases, if any` `the day I ask about`
    WHERE
        `the day the agreement ceases, if any` MEANS IF `the agreement has ceased to be in force` THEN JUST `the day the agreement ceases to be in force` ELSE NOTHING

@export Is the Agreement on Social Security between Canada and the Republic of Poland deemed to have been in force in Canada on a given day (2010, c. 12, s. 1828)?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `2010, c. 12, s. 1828: Was the Agreement with Poland in force in Canada on a day` IF
    `2010, c. 12, s. 1828: the Agreement with the Republic of Poland is deemed to have been in force in Canada on the day` `the day I ask about`

@export Is an action taken under the Agreement with Poland between October 1, 2009 and the day s 1828 came into force deemed lawful (2010, c. 12, s. 1829)?
GIVEN `the action was taken in accordance with the conditions of the Agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the action taken in accordance with the conditions of the Agreement?
      `the day the action was taken` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the action taken?
      `the day section 1828 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 1828 come into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `2010, c. 12, s. 1829: Was an action taken under the Agreement with Poland lawful` IF
    `2010, c. 12, s. 1829: the action is deemed to be lawful` `the action was taken in accordance with the conditions of the Agreement` `the day the action was taken` `the day section 1828 came into force`

@export Do the pre-2007 subparagraphs 11(7)(e)(ii), 19(6)(d)(ii) and 21(9)(c)(ii) still apply to me (2007, c. 11, s. 37)?
GIVEN `before royal assent I was a beneficiary of a supplement or an allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before the day the 2007 Act received royal assent, were you a beneficiary of a supplement or an allowance under the Old Age Security Act?
      `before royal assent I had applied for a supplement or an allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before that day, had you made an application for payment of a supplement or an allowance?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `2007, c. 11, s. 37: Do the old supplement and allowance rules still apply to me` IF
    `2007, c. 11, s. 37: subparagraphs 11(7)(e)(ii), 19(6)(d)(ii) and 21(9)(c)(ii), as they read immediately before royal assent, continue to apply to the person` `before royal assent I was a beneficiary of a supplement or an allowance` `before royal assent I had applied for a supplement or an allowance`

@export Does section 29 as it read before the 2007 amendments still apply to my application (2007, c. 11, s. 38)?
GIVEN `my application was made under section 29 before royal assent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your application made under section 29 before the day the 2007 Act received royal assent?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `2007, c. 11, s. 38: Does the old section 29 still apply to my application` IF
    `2007, c. 11, s. 38: section 29, as it read immediately before royal assent, continues to apply in respect of the application` `my application was made under section 29 before royal assent`

@export Do the repealed provisions of the Canada Pension Plan and the Old Age Security Act still apply to my appeal (2012, c. 19, s. 262)?
GIVEN `a Review Tribunal or the Pension Appeals Board remains seized of my appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a Review Tribunal or the Pension Appeals Board remain seized of your appeal?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `2012, c. 19, s. 262: Do the old appeal provisions still apply to my appeal` IF
    `2012, c. 19, s. 262: the repealed provisions of the Canada Pension Plan and the Old Age Security Act, and their related regulations, continue to apply to the appeal` `a Review Tribunal or the Pension Appeals Board remains seized of my appeal`

-- 2021, c. 23, s. 275 says only that an amount payable to pensioners aged 75 or older on June 30, 2022, under a program for a one-time payment of $500, may be paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund. The program itself is not in the text,
-- so the answer is the amount that may be so paid: it is not a statement that the person is entitled to it.
@export Am I a pensioner to whom the one-time payment of $500 may be paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund (2021, c. 23, s. 275)?
GIVEN `I am a pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a pensioner (a person whose application for a pension has been approved)?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `2021, c. 23, s. 275: Is the one-time $500 payment one that may be paid to me` IS
    `2021, c. 23, s. 275: the amount of the one-time payment to the pensioner that may be paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `I am a pensioner` `my date of birth`
